{
  "comment": "The connector caller token wire (ADR-0168 decision 7, extended by ADR 0178 and ADR 0270 decision 2). The worker mints one per sandbox boot (apps/worker/src/curie_worker/caller_token.py) and the runner presents it to each hosted connector in the X-Curie-Caller header. A verifier holds only the public half, so what it checks must be exactly what the worker signs, and this file freezes that. The token is `cct.<payload>.<signature>`: payload is the base64url, unpadded, of the compact JSON object {agent, exp} with optional {run, work_item} (both or neither) and optional principal, sorted keys at every level and ASCII escapes; signature is the base64url, unpadded, of the 64-byte Ed25519 signature over the ASCII bytes of `cct.<payload>`. `agent` is the stored agent name, verbatim. `exp` is absolute unix seconds. `run` and `work_item` are lowercase hyphenated UUIDs. `principal` (ADR 0270) is the verified human requester, an object with exactly `tenant_id` (a lowercase hyphenated UUID), `issuer` (1 to 2048 characters) and `subject` (1 to 256 characters), compared exactly; these are the bounds of packages/curie-internal/src/curie_internal/identity_context.py ContextCanonicalV1 (`Issuer` and `Identifier`, text that encodes to UTF-8, so a lone surrogate refuses and a control character is carried as a JSON escape) and of its canonical UUID for the tenant, so a principal valid for HTTP identity is valid in the token; it is complete or absent. Each vector carries `seed` (standard base64 of the 32-byte Ed25519 seed the chart's Secret holds), `public` (standard base64 of its 32-byte public key), the claims (a `principal` key holds the three fields), and `minted`. Ed25519 signing is deterministic, so a minter must reproduce `minted` byte for byte. `malformed_principals` are tokens signed under the first vector's seed whose `payload` is the exact JSON text signed, so a duplicate key can be written down; each signature verifies and each token is refused as invalid for its claims. `tampered_principals` are a_human_requester's token with its payload re-encoded after one change, named by `field` (a principal field, or `principal` when it was removed), under the original signature; each is refused as invalid. `forged_principal_headers` names the header only the caller proxy may set (`header`) and requests that forge it on an agent-only token of `token_kind` cct or ccr; `inbound` is the list of [name, value] pairs sent, values fake base64url text. The proxy admits each request and strips every copy before the connector. Readers: apps/worker/tests/test_connector_caller_token.py (the minter: reproduces every `vectors` token, checks the corpus with the primitive, and rejects an unknown key at every level, so a key added for one reader cannot pass vacuously); apps/worker/tests/test_connector_caller_verify.py (the verifier: `vectors`, `malformed_principals`, `tampered_principals`); apps/worker/tests/test_connector_proxy.py (agent-only and principal-bearing vectors by name, sent over a real socket, and the cct `forged_principal_headers` cases); apps/worker/tests/test_connector_proxy_routes.py (a_plain_agent_name's seed and key, a_human_requester's principal, and the ccr `forged_principal_headers` cases); apps/worker/tests/test_connector_proxy_upstream_host.py (a_plain_agent_name); cli/tests/connector_caller_keys.rs (every vector's seed and public).",
